From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:20:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex 0065: the GPU's pending writes in a sorted vector

Every read of a shader's table of resources on the CPU asks whether its word
lies in a range the GPU may still write. Those ranges were a std::map by
start address, scanned from the first range long enough to reach the word
(the longest range ever recorded set that distance) and, for whole-range
questions, from the beginning: 7 % of the command thread in Astro Bot, in
the scan and the tree walk.

PendingGpuWrites keeps them sorted and disjoint (overlapping and touching
ranges merge, with the latest tick), so every question is a binary search:
the range holding a word, whether a range intersects, how many bytes they
cover.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
